@@ -181,6 +182,62 @@ Note: Use the `accountId` from your own `deployment.jsonc`, i.e the account the
 
 In exactly those cases the generated Wrangler config [declares the secret as required](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/secrets/#validate-secrets-before-deploy), so the deploy fails clearly if it is missing. On the default path it does not, so a deployment that needs no token is never blocked waiting for one.
 
+#### Deployment-managed CLIProxy
+
+```jsonc
+"aiGateway": { "enabled": false },
+"sharedAi": {
+  "baseUrl": "https://proxy-api.buchan.cloud/v1",
+  "models": [{ "model": "gpt-5.5", "name": "CLIProxy GPT-5.5" }]
+}
+```
+
+These are implemented deployment controls, not `/admin` settings. The endpoint is fixed and only
+one `gpt-5.5` entry is accepted. `name` is public display text (1–100 characters). No discovery,
+custom headers, credential-name selector, alternate URL or model is supported. Conservative limits
+are **128,000 context / 4,096 output tokens**, with text and tools only; image/PDF requests are
+rejected. These are supported application caps, not a claim about the proxy's full capabilities.
+
+The starter emits nonsecret `SHARED_AI_MODELS` only on Workshop and unions `CLIPROXY_API_KEY` into
+Workshop's `secrets.required`, preserving other requirements. The key must be a **Workshop-only
+Worker secret**, never a JSON var, user provider, frontend flag or Gatekeeper credential. The
+selection identity is `managed:cliproxy:gpt-5.5`; personal `gpt-5.5` records do not collide. Every
+authenticated account can select it within its existing workspace permissions. Provider editing,
+reading credentials, cloning secrets and deleting the managed entry are refused server-side.
+Public metadata contains only managed IDs. Backend references and model-binding props contain no
+shared key; the common model transport resolves the reference and injects the secret immediately
+before the fixed `/v1/responses` request, rejecting redirects and ignoring user Gateway overrides.
+
+Quick-model title/naming requests remain **off until the user opts in** in Providers. Enabling
+this direct catalog does not change existing personal selections, explicit No-agent, Access,
+workspace permissions, or enable Cloudflare limits/billing. CLIProxy usage is paid by the operator's
+proxy arrangement, not by unrelated Cloudflare credits. Gateway quick defaults remain unchanged
+if Gateway is separately enabled.
+
+Before any authorized rollout, confirm the exact Workshop account/name and private routing.
+Provision the first Worker/secret version under deployment approval: `wrangler secret put`
+immediately deploys a version, whereas `wrangler versions secret put` stages a version for a
+separately authorized rollout. A new Worker may require an approved bootstrap identity/version
+before secrets can be installed. Do not bypass `secrets.required` to bootstrap the full app. Never
+put a key in command arguments, logs, reports or source. Missing credentials produce an explicit
+unavailable-credential error; a listed entry is not proof that its credential is installed.
+
+For rotation, privately replace the Workshop secret, roll out and verify the new version, drain
+old/in-flight handles as needed, then revoke the previous upstream key. To disable, omit `sharedAi`
+or use `models: []` and roll out. Saved managed references then fail closed instead of reverting to
+another credential; preferences remain stored, quick titles stop when no longer offered. The
+browser's existing invalid-choice fallback can select another listed model, so verify the picker
+after removal. Removing the catalog or rolling back code does **not** revoke an upstream key.
+
+This feature requires the local OS patch at selected base
+`1045d2e1ceac7be29e1a6f056c936fb31aa00851`; the starter gitlink alone cannot preserve uncommitted
+submodule source. Preserve the patch separately until an authorized commit/upstream integration.
+On upgrades, recheck User catalog/quick resolution, personal mutation guards, `getModel` transport,
+Responses streaming/error handling and public provider metadata/UI. No dependency, Worker or
+migration is added. Local tests use synthetic keys and mocked upstream responses; real two-user
+Access, text/tool continuation, quick/spawn/resume and credential rotation acceptance remain
+post-deployment checks, not something local validation establishes.
+
 ### Observability
 
 The starter enables structured custom logs and a private console-backed Error Reporter, while invocation logs, traces, and browser reporting remain separate controls. See [Observability and error reporting](observability.md) for signal selection, sampling, triage, privacy, source maps, frontend reporting, and external destinations.
